WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:03.051
- [Female Narrator] This
is a baby Cuban Crocodile,

00:00:03.051 --> 00:00:06.134
one of the rarest crocs in the world.

00:00:08.471 --> 00:00:10.693
Hidden away in only two parts of Cuba,

00:00:10.693 --> 00:00:14.081
they have the smallest
range of any croc species.

00:00:14.081 --> 00:00:16.491
The Cuban Crocodile is
critically endangered.

00:00:16.491 --> 00:00:21.011
Experts say approximately
3,000 remain in the wild.

00:00:21.011 --> 00:00:22.761
Its black pebbled scales set it apart

00:00:22.761 --> 00:00:25.150
from the other crocodiles.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.990
They favor freshwater lakes and swamps,

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.171
rarely venturing into the ocean.

00:00:30.171 --> 00:00:32.561
They're strong swimmers,
using their powerful tails

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:35.179
to thrust out of the
water, catching prey hiding

00:00:35.179 --> 00:00:37.761
in overhanging branches.

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:40.129
Habitat degradation,
hunting, and interbreeding

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:44.190
with related crocodile
species all pose threats.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.379
This is a Cuban Crocodile.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.129
(dramatic music)

